  "title": "Cox Automotive Research Reveals the Tax Season Affordability Gap – and Why Hertz Car Sales Has the Answer -",
  "summary": "Tax season is bringing high-intent car buyers to market, but a widening gap between what shoppers want and what they can afford is reshaping purchase decisions in 2026. New data from Cox Automotive shows that more than half of refund-driven buyers are purchasing out of necessity, and most expect to spend well below today’s average new car price of nearly $50,000. Hertz Car Sales is meeting that moment with the largest selection of near-new, model year 2025 vehicles in the U.S. used retail market – priced on average at more than half the cost of buying new.",
